**#4471 holds two causes, not one.** Every report in it is about a wrong date, so they were merged as one
issue — but by the desk's own rule (`causes.ts`) they come from two causes that need two fixes, so each
cause has a ticket of its own: **parser** ([issue #6](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/6))
and **hint** ([issue #5](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/5)).

<Callout>

A cause is decided by **where a report comes from** — the tenant's locale, its booking form and the
channel the report came through — not by its subject, and not by intake's tag (`causes.ts`). Same
subject, different cause is normal here.

</Callout>

## What #4471 really holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

- **parser** — the shared parser reads every date month first, so a day-first tenant's dates come out
  swapped. This is what the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) describes. One fix: read dates in the tenant's order.
- **hint** — booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field; people at day-first tenants type
  what it says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Only reports that came **through the form** from a
  booking-v3 day-first tenant. Fixing the parser does not fix these. Their ticket: [issue #5](https://github.com/wojciechbednarz/mega-s01e03-kb/issues/5).
- **The desk's one-day notes** — the desk read a few reports as a date moving by one day
  (`desk-notes.json`). By the desk's rule (`causes.ts`) they are **parser** reports: counted in the parser
  ticket and footnoted there. [A task](/kb/tasks/fix-time-zone-moves) checks that the parser fix clears them too.

## Why one ticket held two causes

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose **subject lines** match, without
  reading anything else; the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) says "when unsure, merge". Both causes share
  subjects like "Invite came on the wrong day" (see the table).
- Intake's tag is a guess from the browser: some hint reports were tagged `parser`, and the other way round.

Decision 0001 stays as accepted (decisions are never edited). What it should change is proposed in [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-split-by-cause).

## Sources

- `reports-4471.json` — the ticket system's export of 2026-10-04; its pages overlap, so reports are counted once by id.
- `tenants/*.json` — locale and booking form per tenant, which `causes.ts` reads.
- `desk-notes.json` — the reports the desk itself read as a one-day move.

